cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Outcome-aware context allocation: a local experiment in pre-answer evidence budgets"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-16"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/outcome-aware-context-allocation"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/outcome-aware-context-allocation"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research software for selecting two or ten already-available paragraphs before
  a local citation-producing reader answers. An independent 512-question paired
  trial of the same pinned reader with ten paragraphs passed the unchanged
  reader-admission gate: strict benchmark successes increased from 27 to 103 and
  answer exact matches from 260 to 344. A separately registered action study
  found optimistic oracle headroom. A subsequent 512-fit/256-holdout routing
  probe failed its prespecified continuation screen: the outcome-trained
  controller and fixed-ten each had 66 strict successes, with 181 versus 182
  answer matches and only 2.13 percent lower reconstructed seconds per strict
  success. Simpler controls matched or beat the controller under the development
  screen. Further allocation-label expansion under that hypothesis stopped.
  Reader improvement is distinct from useful allocation: no eligible final
  allocation-efficiency interval or operational benefit is demonstrated. The
  release provides isolated protocols, complete continuous request accounting,
  held-out evaluation, aggregate findings and provenance. Raw-result
  authentication requires retained private data, outputs and assets. Historical
  failed/inconclusive results and source bindings remain unchanged.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - context allocation
  - outcome-aware routing
  - evidence budgets
  - reproducible research
  - inconclusive results
